{
    "background_story": "Nayeli was a young Polish immigrant who arrived in the United States with a suitcase full of dreams and a pocket full of grosz, the Polish coins her grandmother had given her for good luck. With only a few dollars to her name, she settled in a small apartment in Brooklyn and began working multiple jobs to make ends meet. Nayeli's determination and strong work ethic quickly earned her a reputation as a reliable and skilled worker. She saved every grosz she could, eventually opening her own small bakery, where she served traditional Polish pastries and bread. As her business grew, so did her reputation as a talented entrepreneur. Nayeli never forgot her humble beginnings and always kept a few grosz in her pocket as a reminder of where she came from and how far she had come.",
